      <h1 data-en="Commission-Based vs Flat-Rate Booking Apps: Which Saves You More?" data-fr="Applications de réservation à commission vs tarif fixe : laquelle vous fait économiser le plus?">Commission-Based vs Flat-Rate Booking Apps: Which Saves You More?</h1>
      <div class="article-meta" data-en="Published June 14, 2026 · 9 min read" data-fr="Publié le 14 juin 2026 · 9 min de lecture">Published June 14, 2026 · 9 min read</div>
    </div>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p data-en="When you go looking for a booking app for your barbershop or salon, you will run into two fundamentally different pricing models. The first charges no monthly fee but takes a percentage of your revenue every time a new client books. The second charges a flat monthly rate — and takes nothing from your bookings." data-fr="Lorsque vous cherchez une application de réservation pour votre barbershop ou salon, vous rencontrerez deux modèles de tarification fondamentalement différents. Le premier ne facture aucun frais mensuel mais prélève un pourcentage de vos revenus à chaque réservation d'un nouveau client. Le second facture un tarif mensuel fixe — et ne prend rien sur vos réservations.">When you go looking for a booking app for your barbershop or salon, you will run into two fundamentally different pricing models. The first charges no monthly fee but takes a percentage of your revenue every time a new client books. The second charges a flat monthly rate — and takes nothing from your bookings.</p>

      <p data-en="Both models have real trade-offs. This article runs the actual math across three realistic shop scenarios — a small solo shop, a growing three-barber shop, and a busy five-barber shop — so you can see exactly where the crossover point is and which model wins at each stage of growth." data-fr="Les deux modèles ont de véritables compromis. Cet article effectue les calculs réels à travers trois scénarios réalistes — un petit salon solo, un salon en croissance avec trois barbiers et un salon multi-barbiers occupé — pour vous montrer exactement où se situe le point de croisement et quel modèle gagne à chaque étape de croissance.">Both models have real trade-offs. This article runs the actual math across three realistic shop scenarios — a small solo shop, a growing three-barber shop, and a busy five-barber shop — so you can see exactly where the crossover point is and which model wins at each stage of growth.</p>

      <h2 data-en="How Commission-Based Booking Apps Work" data-fr="Comment fonctionnent les applications de réservation à commission">How Commission-Based Booking Apps Work</h2>

      <p data-en="The dominant example of a commission-based booking app is Fresha. The model works like this: there is no monthly subscription fee. Instead, Fresha lists your business in their consumer marketplace, and when a brand-new client discovers your business through that marketplace and books an appointment, Fresha charges you 20% of the service price." data-fr="L'exemple dominant d'une application de réservation à commission est Fresha. Le modèle fonctionne ainsi : il n'y a pas de frais d'abonnement mensuel. En revanche, Fresha répertorie votre entreprise dans leur marketplace, et lorsqu'un tout nouveau client découvre votre entreprise via ce marketplace et prend un rendez-vous, Fresha vous facture 20% du prix du service.">The dominant example of a commission-based booking app is Fresha. The model works like this: there is no monthly subscription fee. Instead, Fresha lists your business in their consumer marketplace, and when a brand-new client discovers your business through that marketplace and books an appointment, Fresha charges you <strong>20% of the service price</strong>.</p>

      <p data-en="Returning clients are not charged commission — only first-time bookings. This distinction matters because it means your effective monthly cost is directly tied to how fast your shop is growing. A shop that is growing quickly attracts more new clients, which means more commission fees. The more successful you are at bringing in new business, the more you pay." data-fr="Les clients qui reviennent ne sont pas facturés de commission — seulement les premières réservations. Cette distinction compte car votre coût mensuel effectif est directement lié à la rapidité de croissance de votre salon. Un salon qui croît rapidement attire plus de nouveaux clients, ce qui signifie plus de frais de commission. Plus vous réussissez à attirer de nouvelles affaires, plus vous payez.">Returning clients are not charged commission — only first-time bookings. This distinction matters because it means your effective monthly cost is directly tied to how fast your shop is growing. A shop that is growing quickly attracts more new clients, which means more commission fees. <strong>The more successful you are at bringing in new business, the more you pay.</strong></p>

      <p data-en="Fresha also offers optional paid add-ons — SMS marketing, online payment processing, no-show protection deposits — each with additional fees layered on top of the commission. But the core mechanic is the 20% new-client commission." data-fr="Fresha propose également des modules complémentaires payants optionnels — marketing SMS, traitement des paiements en ligne, dépôts de protection contre les absences — chacun avec des frais supplémentaires s'ajoutant à la commission. Mais le mécanisme principal est la commission de 20% sur les nouveaux clients.">Fresha also offers optional paid add-ons — SMS marketing, online payment processing, no-show protection deposits — each with additional fees layered on top of the commission. But the core mechanic is the 20% new-client commission.</p>

      <h2 data-en="How Flat-Rate Booking Apps Work" data-fr="Comment fonctionnent les applications de réservation à tarif fixe">How Flat-Rate Booking Apps Work</h2>

      <p data-en="A flat-rate booking app charges a predictable fixed fee — monthly or as a one-time lifetime purchase — and takes zero percentage from your bookings. It does not matter whether the client is new or returning, how expensive the service is, or how many appointments you take in a month. The cost stays the same." data-fr="Une application de réservation à tarif fixe facture des frais fixes prévisibles — mensuels ou sous forme d'achat unique à vie — et ne prélève aucun pourcentage sur vos réservations. Peu importe si le client est nouveau ou récurrent, combien coûte le service ou combien de rendez-vous vous prenez dans un mois. Le coût reste le même.">A flat-rate booking app charges a predictable fixed fee — monthly or as a one-time lifetime purchase — and takes zero percentage from your bookings. It does not matter whether the client is new or returning, how expensive the service is, or how many appointments you take in a month. The cost stays the same.</p>

      <p data-en="Bookwize, for example, costs $19/month CAD or $299 as a one-time lifetime payment. Whether you process $500/month in bookings or $50,000/month, your software cost does not change. You keep 100% of every appointment." data-fr="Bookwize, par exemple, coûte 19$/mois CAD ou 299$ en paiement unique à vie. Que vous traitiez 500$ par mois en réservations ou 50 000$ par mois, votre coût logiciel ne change pas. Vous gardez 100% de chaque rendez-vous.">Bookwize, for example, costs $19/month CAD or $299 as a one-time lifetime payment. Whether you process $500/month in bookings or $50,000/month, your software cost does not change. <strong>You keep 100% of every appointment.</strong></p>

      <p data-en="The trade-off: with a flat-rate app, you are responsible for your own client discovery. The app is not a marketplace where new clients browse and find you. Your existing marketing — social media, word of mouth, Google Business profile, your own website — is what brings in new clients. The booking app handles scheduling, reminders, and client management once they arrive." data-fr="Le compromis : avec une application à tarif fixe, vous êtes responsable de la découverte de vos propres clients. L'application n'est pas un marketplace où de nouveaux clients vous trouvent. Votre marketing existant — réseaux sociaux, bouche-à-oreille, profil Google Business, votre propre site web — est ce qui attire de nouveaux clients. L'application de réservation gère la planification, les rappels et la gestion des clients une fois qu'ils arrivent.">The trade-off: with a flat-rate app, you are responsible for your own client discovery. The app is not a marketplace where new clients browse and find you. Your existing marketing — social media, word of mouth, Google Business profile, your own website — is what brings in new clients. The booking app handles scheduling, reminders, and client management once they arrive.</p>

