      <h2 data-en="Frequently Asked Questions" data-fr="Questions fréquentes">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-section">
        <h3 data-en="How does Fresha's commission model work?" data-fr="Comment fonctionne le modèle de commission de Fresha?">How does Fresha's commission model work?</h3>
        <p data-en="Fresha charges a 20% commission on every new client booked through their marketplace. There is no monthly subscription fee, but each time a first-time client discovers and books your business through Fresha, you pay 20% of the service price. Returning clients are not charged commission. This model becomes expensive quickly as your shop grows and attracts more new clients." data-fr="Fresha facture une commission de 20% sur chaque nouveau client réservé via leur marketplace. Il n'y a pas de frais d'abonnement mensuel, mais chaque fois qu'un premier client découvre et réserve votre entreprise via Fresha, vous payez 20% du prix du service. Les clients qui reviennent ne sont pas facturés de commission. Ce modèle devient rapidement coûteux lorsque votre salon se développe et attire plus de nouveaux clients.">Fresha charges a <strong>20% commission</strong> on every new client booked through their marketplace. There is no monthly subscription fee, but each time a first-time client discovers and books your business through Fresha, you pay 20% of the service price. Returning clients are not charged commission. This model becomes expensive quickly as your shop grows and attracts more new clients.</p>

        <h3 data-en="At what point does commission-based pricing cost more than flat-rate?" data-fr="À quel moment la tarification à commission coûte-t-elle plus cher que le tarif fixe?">At what point does commission-based pricing cost more than flat-rate?</h3>
        <p data-en="With Fresha's 20% commission and a flat-rate alternative at $19/month, the break-even point is just 2 new clients per month at an average service price of $50. For example: 2 new clients × $50 × 20% = $20 in commission, which already exceeds the $19/month flat fee. Most active barbershops and salons cross this threshold in their first month of operation." data-fr="Avec la commission de 20% de Fresha et une alternative à tarif fixe à 19$/mois, le seuil de rentabilité est seulement 2 nouveaux clients par mois à un prix de service moyen de 50$. Par exemple : 2 nouveaux clients × 50$ × 20% = 20$ de commission, ce qui dépasse déjà les 19$/mois à tarif fixe. La plupart des barbershops et salons actifs franchissent ce seuil dès leur premier mois d'activité.">With Fresha's 20% commission and a flat-rate alternative at $19/month, the break-even point is just <strong>2 new clients per month</strong> at an average service price of $50. For example: 2 new clients × $50 × 20% = $20 in commission, which already exceeds the $19/month flat fee. Most active barbershops and salons cross this threshold in their first month of operation.</p>

        <h3 data-en="What is a flat-rate booking app?" data-fr="Qu'est-ce qu'une application de réservation à tarif fixe?">What is a flat-rate booking app?</h3>
        <p data-en="A flat-rate booking app charges a fixed monthly fee — or a one-time payment — regardless of how many clients you serve or how much revenue you generate. You pay the same amount whether you have 5 bookings or 500. Unlike commission-based apps, flat-rate apps let you keep 100% of every booking. Bookwize is an example: $19/month or $299 one-time, with zero commission on any booking." data-fr="Une application de réservation à tarif fixe facture des frais mensuels fixes — ou un paiement unique — quel que soit le nombre de clients que vous servez ou le montant de vos revenus. Vous payez le même montant que vous ayez 5 réservations ou 500. Contrairement aux applications à commission, les applications à tarif fixe vous permettent de garder 100% de chaque réservation. Bookwize en est un exemple : 19$/mois ou 299$ en paiement unique, avec zéro commission sur toute réservation.">A <strong>flat-rate booking app</strong> charges a fixed monthly fee — or a one-time payment — regardless of how many clients you serve or how much revenue you generate. You pay the same amount whether you have 5 bookings or 500. Unlike commission-based apps, flat-rate apps let you keep 100% of every booking. Bookwize is an example: $19/month or $299 one-time, with zero commission on any booking.</p>

        <h3 data-en="Should a brand-new shop use a commission-based or flat-rate booking app?" data-fr="Un tout nouveau salon devrait-il utiliser une application de réservation à commission ou à tarif fixe?">Should a brand-new shop use a commission-based or flat-rate booking app?</h3>
        <p data-en="A brand-new shop with zero existing clients and no marketing budget can benefit from the marketplace discovery that commission-based apps like Fresha provide. The trade-off is paying 20% on every new client. However, once a shop consistently books more than 2 new clients per month at average prices, a flat-rate app at $19/month becomes the cheaper option. Most shops should plan to switch to flat-rate within their first 3 to 6 months of operation." data-fr="Un tout nouveau salon sans client existant et sans budget marketing peut bénéficier de la découverte marketplace que des applications à commission comme Fresha offrent. Le compromis est de payer 20% sur chaque nouveau client. Cependant, une fois qu'un salon réserve régulièrement plus de 2 nouveaux clients par mois à des prix moyens, une application à tarif fixe à 19$/mois devient l'option moins chère. La plupart des salons devraient planifier de passer au tarif fixe dans les 3 à 6 premiers mois d'activité.">A brand-new shop with zero existing clients and no marketing budget can benefit from the marketplace discovery that commission-based apps like Fresha provide. The trade-off is paying 20% on every new client. However, once a shop consistently books more than 2 new clients per month at average prices, a flat-rate app at <strong>$19/month</strong> becomes the cheaper option. Most shops should plan to switch to flat-rate within their first 3 to 6 months of operation.</p>
